              "text": "The next NBA game is **Game 3 of the 2026 NBA Finals**. Here are the details of the upcoming matchup:\n\n*   **Matchup:** San Antonio Spurs vs. New York Knicks (Knicks currently lead the series 2\u20130)\n*   **Date & Time:** Monday, June 8, 2026, at 8:30 PM ET\n*   **Location:** Madison Square Garden, New York City, NY\n\nBecause this is a high-profile NBA Finals game, tickets are in high demand. You can purchase tickets through several verified official and secondary marketplaces:\n\n### 1. Official Ticketing\n*   **Ticketmaster:** As the official ticketing partner of the NBA and the New York Knicks, Ticketmaster is the most secure place to buy primary face-value tickets (if any remain) and verified resale tickets directly from other fans. \n*   **NBATickets.com:** The official portal of the NBA, which will redirect you to the authorized primary ticket sellers for the game.\n\n### 2. Major Secondary Resale Marketplaces\nIf official tickets are sold out, you can find a wide selection of seats on major secondary marketplaces. These platforms offer buyer guarantees to ensure your tickets are valid for entry:\n*   **StubHub:** One of the largest ticket marketplaces with a massive selection of resale tickets.\n*   **SeatGeek:** The official ticketing partner of several NBA franchises, known for its \"Deal Score\" system to help you find the best value for your money.\n*   **Vivid Seats:** Another reliable option that offers a rewards program for frequent event-goers.\n\n### Tips for Buying NBA Finals Tickets:\n*   **Compare All-In Pricing:** Ticket prices for the Finals can be highly volatile. Make sure to toggle \"Show prices with fees\" on resale sites so you can compare the actual final cost before checking out.\n*   **Watch the Schedule:** If you are looking for future games in this series, Game 4 will also be at Madison Square Garden on Wednesday, June 10, while Game 5 (if necessary) will return to the Frost Bank Center in San Antonio on Saturday, June 13.",
